

C_nix$ nvcc -ccbin g++ -I../include -m64 -gencode arch=compute_30,code=sm_30 -c -o mandel_hack.o mandel_hack.cu 
C_nix$ nvcc -ccbin g++ -m64 -gencode arch=compute_30,code=sm_30 -o mandel_hack mandel_hack.o -lgomp


Te see the GPU and CPU disagreements from a log file : 

/usr/bin/printf "\ndelta    real                   imaginary              height\n--------------------------------------------------------------\n"; grep '^[0-9]' K4200_16M_samples.log | awk '{printf("%-5s   %-22s %-22s  %s\n", $14, $4, $6, $9)}' | sort -nr | head -20; /usr/bin/printf "\n--------------------------------------------------------------\n\n"


In order to get IEEE754-2008 precision compliance on the GPU use : 

ieee754$ nvcc -ccbin g++ -I../include -m64 -gencode arch=compute_30,code=sm_30 --ftz=false --prec-div=true --prec-sqrt=true -fmad=false -c -o mandel_hack.o mandel_hack.cu 

ieee754$ nvcc -ccbin g++ -m64 -gencode arch=compute_30,code=sm_30 --ftz=false --prec-div=true --prec-sqrt=true -fmad=false -o mandel_hack mandel_hack.o -lgomp


Monitor activity with : 

nvidia-smi -q -d POWER,TEMPERATURE,MEMORY,PIDS -i 0 -l 10


